  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This study reviews literature on empty trip generation across all transport modes and introduces a new continuous measurement framework based on the proportion of unused vehicle capacity rather than a binary empty-or-full classification. It also establishes a cross-modal framework to transfer mitigation strategies between different driver-provided mobility sectors, including public transit, carpooling, taxis, and ride-hailing.",
      "why": "By replacing binary definitions with a continuous capacity metric and mapping cross-modal similarities, the research enables planners to measure the true extent of underutilization and adapt successful reduction strategies from one transport sector to another."
    }
  },
